  "limitations": "Date is TT, not UTC or UT1; input bounds are arithmetic limits, not an assertion of model validity over millions of years. Precession and frame bias only: no nutation, aberration, Earth rotation, polar motion, ephemeris or complete apparent-place calculation. Matrix direction is GCRS -> mean-of-date for column vectors; transpose reverses this orthogonal transform. Scientific use requires a documented epoch/model validity assessment.",
  "port_notes": "Ports eraPmat06 -> eraPfw06/eraObl06 -> eraFw2m, preserving all polynomial coefficients, TT-century calculation and Rz(gamb), Rx(phib), Rz(-psib), Rx(-epsa) source rotation order/sign conventions. Identity construction and row rotation semantics mirror eraIr/eraRx/eraRz. Reports angles as additional transparent intermediates. Does not merely return a generic rotation matrix; the reusable technique is the IAU bias-precession model. Full ERFA and SOFA-derivation notices are retained.",
